  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **St. Stephen** (1 review): Reviewer found it spectacular, lacking the usual mid-song interlude, with the band riding the rhythm [7]\n- **Big Railroad Blues** (1 review): Reviewer singles out the first-set Big Railroad Blues as a highlight [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **If I Had the World to Give**: back after 49 archived shows (818 days); rare: 9 archived performances [9]\n- **A Hard Rain's Gonna Fall**: back after 55 archived shows (830 days); rare: 7 archived performances [9]\n- **Big RxR Blues**: back after 122 archived shows (1540 days); rare: 5 archived performances [9]\n- **Space - Dark Star**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [9]\n- **Lovelight**: back after 77 archived shows (1173 days); rare: 9 archived performances [9]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **dac2021-09-15.AKGmix.toaste.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 183 min; rated 4.83/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Stage volume began very low and grew stronger over the first couple of songs [1]\n- **deadco2021-09-15.deadco2021-09-15**: source not stated; 17 songs; 189 min [2]. Said about its sound: Frequencies below roughly 60Hz were cut about 6dB with a multiband EQ to remove harsh low end from side mics [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Fireworks set off in the parking lot can be heard about 4:12 into Drums; Oteil played drums there [1]\n- During set break the reviewer and another fan stargazed and saw a cloud resembling Jerry's face beneath the moon [6]\n- Long entry line and a phone ticket problem meant reviewer arrived during Brown-Eyed Women, missing about half the first set [7]\n- Reviewer notes the second set covered nearly all of the Live Dead album, minus the closing Bid You Goodnight [7]\n- Reviewer calls it their best Dead & Company show, with high energy after a year-plus Covid break [8]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **dac2021-09-15.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: 3x AKG398 shotguns (L,C,R); 1x AKG394 Figure-8 (L,R); 2x AKG391 cardioids DIN (L,R); 2x AKG392 omnis 4-foot spread (L,R) > Zoom F8 @ 44.1/16 [1]. Also: Recorded with AKG shotgun, figure-8, cardioid and omni mics into a Zoom F8 at 44.1kHz/16-bit; taper's sixth show of the run [1]\n- **deadco2021-09-15.deadco2021-09-15**: source: 3x AKG398 shotguns (L,C,R); 1x AKG394 Figure-8 (L,R); 2x AKG391 cardioids DIN (L,R); 2x AKG392 omnis 4-foot spread (L,R) > Zoom F8 @ 44.1/16 [2]. Also: Mixed into six channels: front, center plus subwoofer, and rear; rear derived from front mix with phase reversed for separation [2]",
